## Fake Authentication / MAC spoofing

Fake Authentication is a technique where you associate with an access point using a spoofed MAC address to allow your wireless card to inject packets into the network.
This is a replay attack which requires capturing a legitimate packet. First set up capturing (see Capturing section)

Replay packet to associate with AP

```bash
aireplay-ng -1 0 -e $ap_name -a $ap_mac -h $local_mac wlan1mon
```
